==Trivia==
*This sub-chapter is based on the fairy tales ''Sleeping Beauty'' and ''Cinderella''.
**Its Japanese name, Nemureru Mori no Nanika (眠れる森の何か, "Something in the Sleeping Forest"), is derived from the Japanese name of ''Sleeping Beauty'', ''Nemureru Mori no Bijo'' (眠れる森の美女, "Beauty in the Sleeping Forest").
*In the Sleeping Forest, [[Theatre of Fear]], [[Imminent Disaster]] and [[Sacred Forest]] are the only sub-chapters to have an animated base in every stage.
**It is also the only sub-chapter to have more than one type of animated base, with three ([[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]], [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]] and [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]]).
*Due to a bug in [[Version 9.8 Update|Version 9.8]] of the [[The Battle Cats|English Version]], it was once possible to access In the Sleeping Forest immediately after clearing [[Laboratory of Relics]].

